  "description": "The 159 Poor Law Unions of Ireland after Glin Union was dissolved on 30 Sep 1891, the last change to the unions before 1901 (the Ballymahon guardians voted to dissolve in 1895, but the Local Government Board did not act). Glin's divisions are placed as the 1911 Limerick report's Glin (formerly Listowel No. 2) and Rathkeale rural districts show them; the Listowel and Rathkeale areas then agree with the 1911 Table 51 within 0.04% and 0.34%. The same 159 unions stood at the 31 Mar 1901 census, but about 21 DEDs changed union in 1898-99 (see Poor Law Unions 31 Mar 1901). Derived from the 5 Apr 1891 map. See Poor Law Unions 5 Apr 1891 for the method and the checks against the printed areas, which apply here. The map is simplified for display by a coverage simplification of the division map, so neighbouring unions keep common edges (95% of divisions lie within 10 m of the full lines); the full-resolution file is among the downloads.",
